HOW REAL AIRCRAFT DETECTS IT 

                         Windshear detection
                                 │
             ┌───────────────────┴────────────────────┐
        PREDICTIVE (PWS)                          REACTIVE
        = weather radar                           = flight computer
        sees it AHEAD (before you enter)          feels it when you're IN it
             │                                         │
   Doppler: measures drop speed               measures airspeed loss, sinking
   drops coming TOWARDS on one side           → "WINDSHEAR WINDSHEAR WINDSHEAR"
   drops going AWAY on the other side         → red WINDSHEAR on PFD
             │                                → pilot: full power, pitch up
   calculates F-FACTOR (how fast you'd
   lose energy). 0.13 or more = danger
             │
   only below 2300 ft, 5 NM ahead
   amber: "Monitor radar display"
   red:   "Go around, windshear ahead"
          "Windshear ahead" (takeoff)



WHAT MY APP DOES PLEASE 

 FlightGear (has NO microburst wind at all)
        │  gives: rain volumes + Cb clouds
        ▼
 YOUR APP (weather.py outflow)
        │
        ├─ Is it a REAL STORM? (has Cumulonimbus cloud)  ── no ──► no microburst
        │        yes
        ├─ Rain stronger than 0.5?                        ── no ──► no microburst
        │        yes
        ├─ Puts a MICROBURST on the storm CORE (most packed clouds)
        │     size: 0.5 - 1.1 NM radius (real: under 2 NM across) ✅
        │     wind: up to 20 m/s outward + downdraft in middle
        │           (stronger with more rain + turbulence)
        │     strongest just above ground, fades by ~1500 ft ✅
        ▼
 YOUR APP (radar.py PWS) = copy of a real PWS
        │
        ├─ below 2300 ft? ──── no ──► nothing
        ├─ looks 5 NM ahead, ±40° ✅
        ├─ wind along beam → F-FACTOR, averaged over ~1 km ✅
        ├─ F ≥ 0.13 AND rain there (drops to measure)? ✅
        ├─ within 3 NM and ±25° → RED WARNING ✅
        ├─ else → AMBER CAUTION ✅
        └─ above 1200 ft → only the icon, no alert ✅



